{"text": "English 47 Maintenance Cleaning WARNING \u2022 Do not use benzene, thinner, or home/car detergent such as Clorox\u2122 for cleaning purposes. They may damage the surface of the refrigerator and cause a fire. \u2022 Do not spray water onto the refrigerator. This may cause electric shock. Regularly use a dry cloth to remove all foreign substances such as dust or water from the power plug terminals and contact points. 1. Unplug the power cord of the refrigerator. 2. Use a moistened soft lint-free cloth or paper towel to clean the refrigerator\u2019s interior and exterior. 3. When done, use a dry cloth or paper towel to dry well. 4. Plug in the power cord of the refrigerator to turn the refrigerator on. NOTE If you have removed any removable parts such as shelves for cleaning, refer to the overall layout in the Refrigerator at a glance section to make sure you have reinserted correctly. Untitled-8 47 2023-03-29 (cid:31)(cid:31) 2:24:15", "source": "D:\\Study\\4_Forth Semester\\AI\\project\\MultiAgent_RAG\\data\\Top Mounted Freezer SpaceMax 304L user_manual.pdf", "page": 46}